                    LICENCE NOT YET SET — MUST BE COMPLETED BEFORE PUBLICATION

    This placeholder exists so the omission is visible rather than silent.

    A repository published with no licence grants the recipient no rights to
    use, modify or redistribute the code. Legal must replace this file with the
    licence text that applies to this delivery before the repository is pushed
    or shared.

    Replace the whole of this file. If the delivery is proprietary and
    client-owned, the text is typically:

        Copyright (c) 2026 <Legal entity name>. All rights reserved.

        This software is provided to <Client> under the terms of the
        engagement agreement between the parties. No licence is granted to
        any other party.

    If it is to be shared more widely, use the full, unmodified text of the
    chosen licence (Apache-2.0 and MIT are the usual choices; Apache-2.0 adds
    an explicit patent grant) from https://spdx.org/licenses/ and add the
    matching `license` field to pyproject.toml.
